hi Kwaku,

1) beta_est depends on each of the beta[j]'s, so since there are P samplers for the beta[j]'s in each iteration, nimblebeta will get called P times.
1a) Side note: If you just need some summary statistic that doesn't place a role directly in the model, it's often best to calculate that post hoc outside of the MCMC.

2) We don't have a basic importance sampler, but we do have a bunch of sequential Monte Carlo algorithms in the nimbleSMC package, some of which involve importance sampling-type calculations. You could look at the code at github.com/nimble-dev/nimbleSMC <http://github.com/nimble-dev/nimbleSMC>, but it's plausible it's complicated enough compared to what you are trying to do that it may be more of a distraction than anything else.

-chris

